$ CONM2 10. with c.g. offset (1.5, -2, 0.7) and inertias I11 5, I21 0.8, I22 7, I31 -0.6, I32 1.1, I33 9 in a rotated
$ CID 5, on grid 1 with rotated CP and CD 7. The products of inertia are moved to the grid and rotated as the inertia
$ tensor (off-diagonal terms -I21, -I31, -I32), not as the matrix of products.
$ Grid 1 carries the CONM2 and is held by six CELAS2 springs (k = 1000, 2000, ... 6000 in its CD components 1-6) to
$ grid 2, which is fixed. Expected eigenvalues of K phi = lambda M phi, from the exact rigid-mass matrix at grid 1:
$   4.463394E+01, 4.705321E+01, 2.038538E+02, 6.541206E+02, 1.850340E+03, 4.605079E+03
SOL 103
CEND
TITLE = CONM2_CID_PRODUCTS_EIGEN
METHOD = 1
BEGIN BULK
EIGR,1,GIV,,,,6
CORD2R,5,,0.,0.,0.,0.3,0.4,0.866,+C5
+C5,1.,0.2,0.1
CORD2R,7,,1.,2.,3.,1.2,1.9,4.,+C7
+C7,2.,2.5,3.1
GRID,1,7,2.,-1.,0.5,7
GRID,2,,10.,0.,0.,,123456
CONM2,4501,1,5,10.,1.5,-2.,0.7,,+M1
+M1,5.,0.8,7.,-0.6,1.1,9.
CELAS2,101,1000.0,1,1,2,1
CELAS2,102,2000.0,1,2,2,2
CELAS2,103,3000.0,1,3,2,3
CELAS2,104,4000.0,1,4,2,4
CELAS2,105,5000.0,1,5,2,5
CELAS2,106,6000.0,1,6,2,6
ENDDATA
